<h2>Indian oilseeds and specialty products</h2>
<p>This category holds some of India's strongest global positions — not in headline volume terms, but in market share. India is the dominant world supplier of guar gum and psyllium husk, became the largest sesame seed exporter in 2023, and is a major groundnut origin supplying Southeast Asian markets.</p>

<p>We export sesame (hulled and natural), groundnut kernels, guar gum, psyllium husk, makhana, jaggery and dehydrated onion and garlic.</p>

<h2>Aflatoxin is the defining compliance issue here</h2>
<p>For groundnut in particular, aflatoxin is the single most important quality parameter. EU and Japanese limits are strict and strictly enforced, and groundnut is inherently among the highest-risk commodities. Pre-shipment testing isn't a nice-to-have on this product — it's the difference between a clean delivery and a destroyed container.</p>
<p>We arrange aflatoxin testing on request and strongly recommend it for any groundnut shipment to a regulated market. {{ site.inspectionStatement }}</p>

<h2>Food grade vs industrial grade</h2>
<p>Guar gum is the clearest example of why grade specification matters in this category. Food-grade guar gum for thickening and stabilising is a different product, at a different price and specification, from industrial-grade guar used in oil and gas drilling fluids. Specify which you need — viscosity, mesh size and purity requirements differ substantially.</p>

<h2>Purity grading</h2>
<p>Most products in this category are sold on purity grades achieved through machine cleaning and sortex colour-sorting — sesame at 99%, 99.5% or 99.95%, groundnut by count and defect tolerance, psyllium by purity percentage. Higher purity costs more to produce, so buy the grade your application actually needs rather than the highest available.</p>

<h2>Which markets buy these products?</h2>
<p>Groundnut kernels go substantially to Indonesia, Vietnam and the Philippines. Guar gum's largest market is the USA, with Russia and Germany following. Dehydrated onion moves to the USA, Brazil and Germany. Individual product pages carry the cited country-level data as they're published.</p>

